ttern:\n- -2,945\n- 171\n- 5,373\n- -585\n\nI'll estimate the AR(1) coefficient for the differenced series, which will help me understand the underlying dynamics of these year-to-year changes. The coefficient will provide insights into how previous differences might predict current differences in treasury holdings.\n\nThe calculation involves finding phi through least squares, which involves carefully tracking the relationship between consecutive differences in the time series.\n\nBy applying the AR(1) model, I forecast the 1983 value at 64,312, which when rounded provides a precise prediction of treasury holdings.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_63471fa712734d3b8bf7c0b1","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"todo__todo_write","arguments":{"content":"- [x] Find treasury ownership survey data for March 31 (1978-1982) for marketable, interest-bearing securities held by commercial banks\n- [x] Extract time series data for each year\n- [x] Fit ARIMA(1,1,0) model to the data\n- [x] Forecast commercial banks' holdings for March 31, 1983\n- [x] Round to nearest whole number and write to answer.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"todo"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
